---
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import { profile } from "../../data/profile";
---

<Section id="about" title="About" index="01">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
    <img
      src="/images/portrait.jpg"
      alt={`Portrait of ${profile.name}`}
      width="320"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="aspect-[4/5] w-full shrink-0 rounded-md border border-[#d9cdb4] object-cover grayscale-[0.15] dark:border-[#3a3122] sm:w-56"
      data-fallback-src="/images/placeholder.svg"
    />
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[#3a3122] dark:text-[#cfc2a7]">
      <p>
        I'm {profile.name}, an {profile.title.toLowerCase()} based in {profile.location}. I like building vision systems that leave the notebook and survive contact with real cameras, real latency,
        and real users.
      </p>
      <p>
        I started in applied computer science and robotics at PXL, then spent four years at Secury360 building the less-glamorous parts of production ML: data pipelines, temporal models, edge-device
        software, and all the glue that makes demos become actual products. It cut false positives by 40%, dropped cloud costs by 25%, and proved to me that the model is not the most important part.
      </p>
      <p>
        These days I split my time between <a href="https://leftfields.be/" class="link-underline hover:text-[#8a3a14] dark:hover:text-[#e07a3e]">LeftFields</a>, where I work on AI systems for
        clients, and
        Padelize, where I joined as fractional CTO after an audit turned into a full rebuild of the core system.
      </p>
      <p class="italic text-[#5a4e36] dark:text-[#b8a987]">I care about useful AI, boring reliability, and good datasets. The best line of code is the one that never gets written — keep it contained, keep it simple, and ship things that do not fall apart when the lighting changes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
